            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0498" n="490" xml:id="pg490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8951: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-11T11:00:00+03:00">March 11, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. British Ambassador confirms information Hare’s number 107.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d495-f1"/> Eden stressed rupture relations with Italy and told
                    Suwaidi he would expect hear something definite this regard on his return London
                    and intimated British help Iraq if action favorable. If not favorable Ambassador
                    says further economic pressure will be exerted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
